WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions for the sketchbook video (sketchbook-video.mp4), from a machine
transcript: whisper.cpp with the large-v3-turbo model. Correct the words
and keep the times; a cue holds up to two lines of about 36 characters.

00:00:00.681 --> 00:00:05.320
Hi, it's Pedro.
So I was thinking here.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:10.120
Anyone can build software
now in an afternoon or so.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:14.940
So why would you still need
a designer like me for that?

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.340
A little bit of a provocation.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:21.490
Can't Claude actually come up
with a design straight away?

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:28.660
Well, yes, it can. Perfectly.
But building is cheap.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:32.060
But that was never
the hard part, was it?

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:36.920
Knowing what to build and why
and even how is the hard part.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:37.870
Because in the end,

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:41.870
if you're creating something
that needs to work for people,

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:46.920
for even machines
or pets or whatever,

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:52.100
the real test is not
if it works on first look.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.660
It always works on first look.

00:00:54.544 --> 00:00:56.970
But if it makes sense
to whoever uses it,

00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:00.623
and AI will happily build
the wrong thing for you.

00:01:02.648 --> 00:01:07.370
That's for sure. Out of the mega
normalization of what already exists

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.320
and what it consumed.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:15.955
So I start here with questions
about the product, not the code.

00:01:15.955 --> 00:01:19.160
Who is it for?
What are users trying to do?

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.980
How will we know it
works in the end?

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:24.100
How will we measure that?

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.060
So AI and generative coding can
come after that. And it's fast.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:29.810
But thinking about what to make

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:35.940
and why and how is what makes
that speed worth it in the long run.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:42.300
So to make users happy to spend
their time with confidence,

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.120
with confidence in your application.

00:01:46.822 --> 00:01:48.620
Thanks for listening.
Have a nice one.

